1
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:09,860
He wore a suit, she wore the white,

2
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,550
They stood beneath a church-house light.

3
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,860
The preacher spoke, the families cried,

4
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:20,250
They promised God they'd never divide.

5
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:23,780
But somewhere down those passing years,

6
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:27,250
Love turned to silence, trust to tears.

7
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:30,880
Two rings came off, two doors slammed shut,

8
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:34,650
And forever wasn't long enough.

9
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:40,050
Two young women met back when

10
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:43,050
The world was colder to them then.

11
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:46,820
No crowded church, no cheering room,

12
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:50,440
Just trembling hands and borrowed blooms.

13
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:53,840
They built a life through fifty years,

14
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:57,260
Through losing friends and burying fears.

15
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:00,740
Through sickness, bills, and growing old,

16
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:04,240
One kept the other when nights got cold.

17
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,220
So if Heaven saw the whole thing,

18
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:10,850
Not the names, not what we're told—

19
00:01:11,430 --> 00:01:14,060
If God looked past the outside

20
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:17,220
And straight into the soul...

21
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:19,900
Which love would You choose, Lord?

22
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:22,800
The one that looked right from the pew?

23
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:27,450
Or the one that stayed for fifty years

24
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:31,320
When staying was the hardest thing to do?

25
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:34,480
Would You count who held whose hand,

26
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:37,880
Or every promise they lived through?

27
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:41,660
If love is patient, love is kind—

28
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:47,450
Tell me, which love would You choose?

29
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:03,450
They've got silver in their hair now,

30
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:06,800
Photographs across the wall.

31
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:10,040
One still reaches for the other

32
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:13,180
Every time she starts to fall.

33
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,900
They've watched the whole world change outside,

34
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,660
Still wake up sleeping side by side.

35
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:22,920
Fifty winters, fifty springs—

36
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:27,180
Still wearing those two simple rings.

37
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:30,600
Would God turn from a lifetime

38
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:33,800
Of mercy, sacrifice, and truth?

39
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:37,360
Would Heaven call devotion wrong

40
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:40,200
Because it didn't look like you?

41
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:43,760
Maybe we've been asking Heaven

42
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:47,080
To defend the lines we drew.

43
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:50,640
Maybe God sees something deeper

44
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:54,220
Than the things that people do.

45
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:57,540
Maybe when He measures love,

46
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:06,050
He measures what it carried through.

47
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:12,400
So which love would You choose, Lord?

48
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:15,100
I won't pretend I speak for You.

49
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:19,880
But I can't believe You'd hate a heart

50
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:23,220
For loving faithfully and true.

51
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:26,660
One had every blessing people gave

52
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:30,240
And still their forever came unglued.

53
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:33,820
Two held on for fifty years—

54
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:40,300
Tell me, which love would You choose?

55
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:48,850
If I meet You when this life is done,

56
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:55,200
There's one thing I would ask of You:

57
00:03:56,380 --> 00:04:01,100
Did we spend our lives judging love...

58
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:08,000
while You were looking at what love could do?
